al-paragraph \\\"$P\\\" 01-create-button-chain 11.1 '\\\"'Not applicable. This goal owns five work units, within the 2-10 work-unit limit.'\\n\\\\\\\"\\\"'$S/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --goal-section \\\"$P\\\" 02-verify-and-handoff current-state -p '\\\"'2.1: This goal depends on the implementation handoff from 01-create-button-chain. No browser verification is run during the current planning-only proof.'\\n\\\\\\\"\\\"'$S/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --goal-section \\\"$P\\\" 02-verify-and-handoff why -p '\\\"'4.1: The requested behavior is user-facing and needs direct browser-click evidence after implementation, plus clear pass/fail criteria for the completion state.'\\n\\\\\\\"\\\"'$S/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --goal-section \\\"$P\\\" 02-verify-and-handoff scope -p '\\\"'5.1: In scope: execute US-01 after implementation, record click evidence, verify exact append counts, verify document clearing, verify exact lowercase finished text, verify visible white border, and record handoff evidence.' -p '5.2: Out of scope: changing implementation during the verification step, using console or injected events, weakening the story, or marking UI evidence passed during this planning-only proof.'\\n\\\\\\\"\\\"'$S/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --goal-section \\\"$P\\\" 02-verify-and-handoff affected-areas -p '\\\"'6.1: Verification work unit W05 has no implementation file and exercises the future rendered button-chain.html through browser clicks only.'\\n\\\\\\\"\\\"'$S/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --goal-section \\\"$P\\\" 02-verify-and-handoff dependencies -p '\\\"'7.1: W05 depends on W01, W02, W03, W04, and W06. Completion handoff is the recorded US-01 result, bug-register state, and final acceptance evidence.'\\n\\\\\\\"\\\"'$S/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --goal-section \\\"$P\\\" 02-verify-and-handoff approach -p '\\\"'8.1: Run the configured UI story cache after the future HTML exists. Stop on the first unexpected result, record a bug row with reproduction evidence, and add 